# `may not` reads two ways, as a prohibition (`the name may not be a
# dot`) or as a possibility (`the cache may not be warm`), and the
# kubernetes docs use both. The fix writes `must not` for a prohibition
# and `might not` for a possibility. `may or may not` counts too,
# because it ends in the same words and hedges the claim as well.
#
# It hit 55 lines in the kubernetes and nix.dev docs, and all 10
# sampled hits allowed either reading.
expr main may not
let message "May not. Write must not for a prohibition, or might not for a possibility."
let description "Flags may not, which reads as a prohibition or as a possibility."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "The name must not be a dot."
allows "The cache might not be warm."
